Pull raw publish-queue lookup parity (2026-10-13 10:23 UTC):
- Implemented `PullConsumer::fetch_publish_message_queues` for `DefaultMQPullConsumerImpl.fetchPublishMessageQueues`. It passes the caller's topic unchanged, returns writable queues in Java route order, strips the configured namespace from returned queues, and distinguishes the Java missing/empty-route message from wrapped query/conversion failures.
- Source review caught and corrected an initial design that would have used the shared route-refresh path. Java `MQAdminImpl.fetchPublishMessageQueues` queries NameServer directly and does not publish the result into the shared route cache; `ClientRuntime::get_topic_publish_queues` now performs direct API lookup and conversion without cache updates or consumer callbacks.
- Added scripted NameServer coverage for exact topic, queue ordering, repeated lookup, a route disappearing after success, absent/empty routes, malformed route data, and Java error text; core test confirms direct lookup leaves the route cache empty. Updated Phase 6 and Phase 9 mappings.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --locked` (all core unit/integration/doc targets); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` (168 unit tests and all consumer integration/doc targets); targeted direct-cache test; consumer admin integration target (8 tests); strict all-target/all-feature Clippy for core and consumer; formatting and diff checks.
- No live Broker or Docker was used. P9-V03 live validation and the remaining raw implementation audit, including P18-V01, remain open.
